meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: International Migrant Stock
    description: |-
      The estimates of the number (or "stock") of international migrants disaggregated by age, sex and country or area of origin are based on national statistics, in most cases obtained from population censuses. Additionally, population registers and nationally representative surveys provided information on the number and composition of international migrants.

      The dataset presents estimates of international migrant by age, sex and origin. Estimates are presented for 1990, 1995, 2000, 2005, 2010, 2015 and 2020 and are available for 232 countries and areas of the world. The estimates are based on official statistics on the foreign-born or the foreign population.
    date_published: "2020"
    version_producer: 2020 - POP/DB/MIG/Stock/Rev.2020
    title_snapshot: International Migrant Stock - feed of the migrant-demographics visualization
    description_snapshot: |-
      Our World in Data built this file from International Migrant Stock 2020 outside of the ETL, and published it by hand so that the "migrant-demographics" bespoke visualization could fetch it. It carries, per entity and year, the migrant stock by sex and five-year age band alongside the total resident population on the same bands (taken from World Population Prospects), from which the visualization derives the native-born population. Entities without a World Population Prospects population estimate, and entities reporting no migrant stock in any year, were dropped when the file was built.

      This snapshot captures the file exactly as it was being served, so that the feed can be published from the ETL without a byte of it changing. It is an interim measure: once the feed is built from the garden datasets behind those two sources, this snapshot has no reason to exist.

    # Citation
    producer: United Nations Department of Economic and Social Affairs
    citation_full: |-
      United Nations Department of Economic and Social Affairs, Population Division (2020). International Migrant Stock 2020.
    attribution_short: UN DESA

    # Files
    url_main: https://www.un.org/development/desa/pd/content/international-migrant-stock
    # Our World in Data's own copy, not the producer's file: this snapshot exists to capture the
    # hand-published feed as served, and the producer publishes no equivalent of it.
    url_download: https://owid-public.owid.io/bespoke/migrant-demographics/migrant-demographics.json
    date_accessed: "2026-09-17"

